{
 "section": "adversarial preflight, requested by the coordinator before Wave 3",
 "assumption_under_test": "THE COMPARISON CEILING. The whole EXACT_PARALLEL / VARIANT distinction is defined relative to a per-pair ceiling. If the ceiling is computed wrong for one layer combination, edges move between EXACT and VARIANT wholesale -- so it carries more downstream weight than any single figure.",
 "why_this_one": "the 150-pair accent-notation finding was a result ABOUT pairs, not a test OF the ceiling function. Two claims the function makes were never tested: that the ceiling is never too LOW (no pair identical above it), and that the predicted ceiling is actually REACHABLE for each layer combination. The second is where a self-inflicted error hides, because an unreachable ceiling silently demotes every pair a rung and types real exact parallels as variants.",
 "test_A_ceiling_never_too_low": {
  "probe": "for all 2,211 identity rows, recompute the ceiling and assert IDX(match_level) >= IDX(ceiling) and that the stored label agrees",
  "expected": "0 failures",
  "returned": 0,
  "verdict": "HOLDS"
 },
