  "the first digit-only test ignored whitespace, which admitted 12 WORD_DIVISION pairs whose real difference is a space. Whitespace IS word division. Strict test: 139, not 151.",
  "my first difference class lumped digits with dandas, which would have moved 18 Samavedic rows that contain no digit at all -- they differ in ASCII '|' against Devanagari danda (9) or an inserted space (9). Those are genuine apparatus and stay VARIANT.",
